\title{Last digit in base 10}
\date{2026-03-04T03:03:10Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Example}
\p{Under the [equivalence relation #{R_7}](008E), where natural numbers are equivalent if they have the same last digit in base #{10}, the [equivalence class](0097) of #{1} is the infinite set ##{[1] = \{ 1, 11, 21, 31, \dots \}.}}


